    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1103">

                <pb facs="1400" n="1390" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363/10–2946</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-10-29T15:00:00-05:00">October 29, 1946—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>948. Dept recently informed that Anglo-Iranian Oil Co. has signed contract with
                    Chinese Petroleum Corp for delivery Takao of 300,000 tons crude—one-third first
                    half and two-thirds second half 1947. According BritEmb here business taken on
                    competitive bid. According Arabian American Oil, the supposed other bidder, no
                    real bid called for. Aramco consulted by Chinese but when time for bid arrived
                    found business already placed with AIOC. Report requested details especially
                    names of bidders, prices, terms, duration and possible tangential
                    considerations.</p>
                <p>Assumption by AIOC of supervision of rehabilitation Takao refinery (Shanghai
                    A–684, Sept 17<anchor n="19" xml:id="d1103-f1"/>) assumedly in conjunction with
                    crude contract raises question whether Chinese-AIOC arrangement envisages more
                    than mere supply contract. Indications from oil Cos that AIOC interested
                    marketing. Is AIOC financing any part Takao reconstruction? Is AIOC interested
                    in Kansu development?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
